# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Credentials. The GitHub App private key belongs OUTSIDE this working copy entirely
# (see .portulan/tools/README.md); this is the second line of defence, not the first —
# an ignore rule protects against `git add`, never against a future edit to this file.
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# Node / build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Local-only build-session scaffolding — NOT product, and may reference private
# context. Kept on this workstation; never tracked or pushed. (See docs/plan.md.)
/BOOTSTRAP.md
/_local/

# `.claude/` is now PARTLY tracked: `.claude/settings.json` is the compiled enforcement
# (milestone 4) and belongs in review, and so does `.claude/rules/portulan/`, the compiled
# guidance with this repository's boot card in it. Everything else the host puts there is local
# session state. Ignoring the siblings rather than the directory is deliberate — a blanket
# `/.claude/` would silently exclude the generated gate file, and a gate nobody can see in a diff
# is the failure this whole rail exists against.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/rules/
/.claude/rules/*
!/.claude/rules/portulan/

# The constitution + plan live ONLY in docs/ (docs/vision.md + docs/plan.md) — single
# canonical source. These root-level guards ensure that if a vision.md or plan.md ever
# reappears at the repo root, it can never be tracked or pushed.
/vision.md
/plan.md

# This repository keeps no handoff index (`node cli/index.mjs --handoffs .portulan` prints it): a
# committed copy conflicted on every merge that added a handoff, and it carries nothing the series
# does not. With no copy, `index --check` renders it, which proves every handoff yields a line.
/.portulan/handoffs-index.md
